@startuml

title Withdrawing a published set: raise, decide, apply, tell

actor "Trader\n(maker)" as maker
participant "Market data" as md
participant "Inbox\n(library, same database)" as inbox
actor "Decider\n(checker)" as checker
participant "Readers" as readers

== Raise ==
maker -> md : raise withdrawal(publish, reason code, commentary)
md -> md : the set is published and not withdrawn;\nno withdrawal of it is open;\nits kind name a withdrawal kind
md -> inbox : write the request under the kind,\nwith the party and the reason
inbox --> md : the rule in force, if any

== Decide ==
alt a stated rule closes it
  inbox -> inbox : approve, decided by the system
  md -> md : apply (below), in the raise's transaction
else a person decides
  inbox -> checker : a withdrawal waits
  checker -> inbox : approve or refuse (not the maker)
  inbox -> maker : the request is approved
end

== Apply ==
maker -> md : apply withdrawal(request), within the window
md -> md : the request is approved and in its window;\nthe set is not withdrawn yet
group one transaction
  md -> md : mark the set withdrawn: the account,\nthe instant, the reason, the request
  md -> md : write the notice (outbox row)
end
md -> readers : deliver the notice after the commit\n(retried until delivered)
md --> maker : withdrawn

note over md
  The set keeps its values, its publisher and its
  instant. A read by as-of skips it and takes the
  newest remaining set at or before the as-of, so
  withdrawing the live set makes the set it had
  superseded live again.
end note

@enduml
